#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:1
msgid ""
"Page about the mix blending modes in Krita: Allanon, Alpha Darken, Behind, "
"Erase, Geometric Mean, Grain Extract, Grain Merge, Greater, Hard Mix, Hard "
"Overlay, Interpolation, Interpolation2x, Normal, Overlay, Parallel, Penumbra "
"A, B, C and D."
msgstr ""
"Sida om blandningslägen i Krita: Allt igen, Gör alfa mörkare, Bakom, Radera, "
"Geometriskt medelvärde, Extrahera ådring, Sammanfoga ådring, Större än, Hård "
"blandning, Hård överlagring, Interpolation, Interpolation - 2X, Normal, "
"Överlagra, Parallell, Halvskugga A, B, C och D."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:17
msgid "Mix"
msgstr "Blanda"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:19
#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:23
msgid "Allanon"
msgstr "Allt igen"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:27
msgid "This blending mode is called \"Allanon\" in English."
msgstr "Blandningsläget kallas \"Allanon\" på engelska."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:29
msgid ""
"Blends the upper layer as half-transparent with the lower. (It add the two "
"layers together and then halves the value)."
msgstr ""
"Blandar det övre lagret som halvgenomskinligt med det undre (det adderar de "
"två lagren och halverar sedan värdet)."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:34
msgid ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Allanon_Sample_image_with_dots.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Allanon_Sample_image_with_dots.png"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:34
msgid "Left: **Normal**. Right: **Allanon**."
msgstr "Vänster: **Normal**. Höger: **Allt igen**."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:36
#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:40
msgid "Interpolation"
msgstr "Interpolation"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:44
msgid "This blending mode is called \"Interpolation\" in English."
msgstr "Blandningsläget kallas \"Interpolation\" på engelska."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:46
msgid ""
"Subtract 0.5f by 1/4 of cosine of base layer subtracted by 1/4 of cosine of "
"blend layer assuming 0-1 range. The result is similar to Allanon mode, but "
"with more contrast and functional difference to 50% opacity."
msgstr ""
"Subtraherar 0,5f med 1/4 av cosinus av baslagret, subtraherat med 1/4 av "
"cosinus av blandningslagret, med antagandet att intervallet är 0 - 1. "
"Resultatet liknar Allt igen, men med större kontrast och funktionell "
"skillnad mot 50 % ogenomskinlighet."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:52
msgid ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Interpolation_Sample_image_with_dots.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Interpolation_Sample_image_with_dots.png"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:52
msgid "Left: **Normal**. Right: **Interpolation**."
msgstr "Vänster: **Normal**. Höger: **Interpolation**."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:54
msgid "Interpolation2x"
msgstr "Interpolation 2X"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:58
msgid "Interpolation - 2X"
msgstr "Interpolation - 2X"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:62
msgid "This blending mode is called \"Interpolation - 2X\" in English."
msgstr "Blandningsläget kallas \"Interpolation - 2X\" på engelska."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:64
msgid ""
"Applies Interpolation blend mode to base and blend layers, then duplicate to "
"repeat interpolation blending."
msgstr ""
"Utför interpolationsblandning med bas- och blandningslagren, och duplicerar "
"för att upprepa interpolationsblandning."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:69
msgid ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Interpolation_X2_Sample_image_with_dots.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Interpolation_X2_Sample_image_with_dots.png"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:69
msgid "Left: **Normal**. Right: **Interpolation - 2X**."
msgstr "Vänster: **Normal**. Höger: **Interpolation - 2X**."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:71
#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:75
msgid "Alpha Darken"
msgstr "Gör alfa mörkare"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:79
msgid "This blending mode is called \"Alpha Darken\" in English."
msgstr "Blandningsläget kallas \"Alpha Darken\" på engelska."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:81
msgid ""
"As far as I can tell this seems to premultiply the alpha, as is common in "
"some file-formats."
msgstr ""
"Så vitt jag kan se, verkar det multiplicera alfa i förväg, som är vanligt i "
"vissa filformat."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:86
msgid ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Alpha_Darken_Sample_image_with_dots.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Alpha_Darken_Sample_image_with_dots.png"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:86
msgid "Left: **Normal**. Right: **Alpha Darken**."
msgstr "Vänster: **Normal**. Höger: **Gör alfa mörkare**."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:88
#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:92
msgid "Behind"
msgstr "Bakom"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:96
msgid "This blending mode is called \"Behind\" in English."
msgstr "Blandningsläget kallas \"Behind\" på engelska."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:98
msgid ""
"Does the opposite of normal, and tries to have the upper layer rendered "
"below the lower layer."
msgstr ""
"Gör motsatsen av normal, och försöker återge det övre lagret bakom det undre "
"lagret."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:103
msgid ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Behind_Sample_image_with_dots.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Behind_Sample_image_with_dots.png"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:103
msgid "Left: **Normal**. Right: **Behind**."
msgstr "Vänster: **Normal**. Höger: **Bakom**."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:105
msgid "Erase (Blending Mode)"
msgstr "Radera (blandningsläge)"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:109
msgid "Erase"
msgstr "Radera"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:113
msgid "This blending mode is called \"Erase\" in English."
msgstr "Blandningsläget kallas \"Erase\" på engelska."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:115
msgid ""
"This subtracts the opaque pixels of the upper layer from the lower layer, "
"effectively erasing."
msgstr ""
"Subtraherar de ogenomskinliga bildpunkterna på det övre lagret från det "
"undre lagret, vilket betyder att de raderas."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:120
msgid ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Erase_Sample_image_with_dots.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Erase_Sample_image_with_dots.png"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:120
msgid "Left: **Normal**. Right: **Erase**."
msgstr "Vänster: **Normal**. Höger: **Radera**."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:122
#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:126
msgid "Geometric Mean"
msgstr "Geometriskt medelvärde"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:130
msgid "This blending mode is called \"Geometric Mean\" in English."
msgstr "Blandningsläget kallas \"Geometric Mean\" på engelska."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:132
msgid ""
"This blending mode multiplies the top layer with the bottom, and then "
"outputs the square root of that."
msgstr ""
"Blandningsläget multiplicerar det övre lagret med det undre, och matar sedan "
"ut kvadratroten av det."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:137
msgid ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Geometric_Mean_Sample_image_with_dots.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Geometric_Mean_Sample_image_with_dots.png"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:137
msgid "Left: **Normal**. Right: **Geometric Mean**."
msgstr "Vänster: **Normal**. Höger: **Geometriskt medelvärde**."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:139
#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:143
msgid "Grain Extract"
msgstr "Extrahera ådring"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:147
msgid "This blending mode is called \"Grain Extract\" in English."
msgstr "Blandningsläget kallas \"Grain Extract\" på engelska."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:149
msgid ""
"Similar to subtract, the colors of the upper layer are subtracted from the "
"colors of the lower layer, and then 50% gray is added."
msgstr ""
"I likhet med subtrahera, subtraheras färgerna på det övre lagret från "
"färgerna på det undre lagret, och sedan adderas 50 % grått."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:154
msgid ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Grain_Extract_Sample_image_with_dots.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Grain_Extract_Sample_image_with_dots.png"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:154
msgid "Left: **Normal**. Right: **Grain Extract**."
msgstr "Vänster: **Normal**. Höger: **Extrahera ådring**."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:156
#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:160
msgid "Grain Merge"
msgstr "Sammanfoga ådring"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:164
msgid "This blending mode is called \"Grain Merge\" in English."
msgstr "Blandningsläget kallas \"Grain Merge\" på engelska."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:166
msgid ""
"Similar to addition, the colors of the upper layer are added to the colors, "
"and then 50% gray is subtracted."
msgstr ""
"I likhet med addition, adderas färgerna på det övre lagret från färgerna på "
"det undre lagret, och sedan subtraheras 50 % grått."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:171
msgid ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Grain_Merge_Sample_image_with_dots.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Grain_Merge_Sample_image_with_dots.png"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:171
msgid "Left: **Normal**. Right: **Grain Merge**."
msgstr "Vänster: **Normal**. Höger: **Sammanfoga ådring**."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:173
msgid "Greater (Blending Mode)"
msgstr "Större än (blandningsläge)"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:177
msgid "Greater"
msgstr "Större än"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:181
msgid "This blending mode is called \"Greater\" in English."
msgstr "Blandningsläget kallas \"Greater\" på engelska."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:183
msgid ""
"A blending mode which checks whether the painted color is painted with a "
"higher opacity than the existing colors. If so, it paints over them, if not, "
"it doesn't paint at all."
msgstr ""
"Ett blandningsläge som kontrollerar om den målade färgen målas med en större "
"ogenomskinlighet än de befintliga färgerna, och om så är fallet målar det "
"över dem. Om inte, målar det inte alls."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:188
#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:192
msgid "Hard Mix"
msgstr "Hård blandning"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:196
msgid "This blending mode is called \"Hard Mix\" in English."
msgstr "Blandningsläget kallas \"Hard Mix\" på engelska."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:198
msgid "Similar to Overlay."
msgstr "Liknar Överlagra."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:200
msgid ""
"Mixes both Color Dodge and Burn blending modes. If the color of the upper "
"layer is darker than 50%, the blending mode will be Burn, if not the "
"blending mode will be Color Dodge."
msgstr ""
"Blandar båda blandningslägen färgblekning och bränn. Om färgen på det övre "
"lagret är mörkare än 50 %, är blandningsläget bränn, om inte är "
"blandningsläget färgblekning."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:206
msgid ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Hard_Mix_Sample_image_with_dots.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Hard_Mix_Sample_image_with_dots.png"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:206
msgid "Left: **Normal**. Right: **Hard Mix**."
msgstr "Vänster: **Normal**. Höger: **Hårt blandning**."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:208
#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:212
msgid "Hard Mix (Photoshop)"
msgstr "Hård blandning (Photoshop)"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:216
msgid "This blending mode is called \"Hard Mix (Photoshop)\" in English."
msgstr "Blandningsläget kallas \"Hard Mix (Photoshop)\" på engelska."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:218
msgid "This is the hard mix blending mode as it is implemented in photoshop."
msgstr ""
"Det här är blandningsläget hård blandning som det är implementerat i "
"Photoshop."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:224
msgid ".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/Krita_4_0_hard_mix_ps.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/Krita_4_0_hard_mix_ps.png"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:224
msgid ""
"**Left**: Dots are mixed in with the normal blending mode, on the **Right**: "
"Dots are mixed in with hardmix."
msgstr ""
"**Vänster**: Punkter blandas in med det normala blandningsläget, till "
"**Höger**: Punkter blandas in med hård blandning."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:226
msgid ""
"This add the two values, and then checks if the value is above the maximum. "
"If so it will output the maximum, otherwise the minimum."
msgstr ""
"Det lägger ihop de två värdena och kontrollerar sedan om resultatet är "
"ovanför maximum. I så fall matas maximum ut, annars minimum."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:228
#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:232
msgid "Hard Mix Softer (Photoshop)"
msgstr "Hård blandning mjukare (Photoshop)"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:236
msgid ""
"This blending mode is called \"Hard Mix Softer (Photoshop)\" in English."
msgstr "Blandningsläget kallas \"Hard Mix Softer (Photoshop)\" på engelska."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:240
msgid ""
"This is the hard mix blending mode as it is implemented in photoshop for "
"texturing brushes. It produces softer edges than the normal *Hard Mix "
"(Photoshop)*."
msgstr ""
"Det här är blandningsläget hård blandning som det är implementerat i "
"Photoshop för strukturpenslar. Den ger mjukare kanter än det vanliga *Hård "
"blandning (Photoshop)*."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:247
msgid ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Hard_Mix_Softer_Photoshop_Sample_image_with_dots.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Hard_Mix_Softer_Photoshop_Sample_image_with_dots.png"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:247
msgid ""
"**Left**: Dots are mixed in with the normal blending mode, on the **Right**: "
"Dots are mixed in with hard mix softer."
msgstr ""
"**Vänster**: Punkter blandas in med det normala blandningsläget, till "
"**Höger**: Punkter blandas in med hård blandning mjukare."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:249
msgid ""
"This is like the inverse subtract mode but the two terms are scaled up to "
"increase the contrast. This is not really a hard mix mode in the sense that "
"it doesn't choose between a result or another based on a threshold, although "
"in most cases the result looks like the normal *Hard Mix (Photoshop)* but "
"with softer edges."
msgstr ""
"Liknar omvänd subtraktion men de två termerna skalas upp för att öka "
"kontrasten. Det är egentligen inte ett hårt blandningsläge i den mening att "
"det inte väljer mellan ett resultat och ett annat baserat på en tröskel, "
"även om resultatet ser ut som det vanliga *Hård blandning (Photoshop)* men "
"med mjukare kanter i de flesta fall."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:253
#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:257
msgid "Hard Overlay"
msgstr "Hård överlagring"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:261
msgid "This blending mode is called \"Hard Overlay\" in English."
msgstr "Blandningsläget kallas \"Hard Overlay\" på engelska."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:265
msgid ""
"Similar to Hard light but hard light use Screen when the value is above 50%. "
"Divide gives better results than Screen, especially on floating point images."
msgstr ""
"Liknar Hårt ljus, men hårt ljus använder Skärm när värdet är över 50 %. "
"Dividera ger bättre resultat än Skärm, särskilt för flyttalsbilder."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:270
msgid ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Hard_Overlay_Sample_image_with_dots.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Hard_Overlay_Sample_image_with_dots.png"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:270
msgid "Left: **Normal**. Right: **Hard Overlay**."
msgstr "Vänster: **Normal**. Höger: **Hård överlagring**."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:272
msgid "Normal (Blending Mode)"
msgstr "Normal (blandningsläge)"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:272
msgid "Source Over"
msgstr "Källa över"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:276
msgid "Normal"
msgstr "Normal"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:280
msgid "This blending mode is called \"Normal\" in English."
msgstr "Blandningsläget kallas \"Normal\" på engelska."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:282
msgid ""
"As you may have guessed this is the default Blending mode for all layers."
msgstr "Som man kan gissa är det standardblandningsläge för alla lager."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:284
msgid ""
"In this mode, the computer checks on the upper layer how transparent a pixel "
"is, which color it is, and then mixes the color of the upper layer with the "
"lower layer proportional to the transparency."
msgstr ""
"Med läget, kontrollerar datorn på det övre lagret hur genomskinlig en "
"bildpunkt är, vilken färg den har, och blandar det övre lagrets färg med det "
"undre lagret proportionellt mot genomskinligheten."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:289
msgid ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Normal_50_Opacity_Sample_image_with_dots.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Normal_50_Opacity_Sample_image_with_dots.png"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:289
msgid "Left: **Normal** 100% Opacity. Right: **Normal** 50% Opacity."
msgstr ""
"Vänster: **Normal** 100 % ogenomskinlighet. Höger: **Normal** 50 % "
"ogenomskinlighet."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:291
msgid "Overlay (Blending Mode)"
msgstr "Överlagra (blandningsläge)"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:295
msgid "Overlay"
msgstr "Överlagra"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:299
msgid "This blending mode is called \"Overlay\" in English."
msgstr "Blandningsläget kallas \"Overlay\" på engelska."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:301
msgid ""
"A combination of the Multiply and Screen blending modes, switching between "
"both at a middle-lightness."
msgstr ""
"En kombination av blandningslägena Multiplicera och Skärm, som byter mellan "
"de båda vid mittljushet."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:303
msgid ""
"Overlay checks if the color on the upperlayer has a lightness above 0.5. If "
"so, the pixel is blended like in Screen mode, if not the pixel is blended "
"like in Multiply mode."
msgstr ""
"Överlagra kontrollerar om färgen på det övre lagret har en ljushet över 0,5. "
"Om så är fallet, blandas bildpunkten som i läget Skärm, annars blandas "
"bildpunkten som i läget Multiplikation."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:305
msgid "This is useful for deepening shadows and highlights."
msgstr "Det är användbart för att göra skuggor och dagrar djupare."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:310
msgid ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Overlay_Sample_image_with_dots.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Overlay_Sample_image_with_dots.png"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:310
msgid "Left: **Normal**. Right: **Overlay**."
msgstr "Vänster: **Normal**. Höger: **Överlagra**."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:312
#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:316
msgid "Parallel"
msgstr "Parallell"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:320
msgid "This blending mode is called \"Parallel\" in English."
msgstr "Blandningsläget kallas \"Parallel\" på engelska."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:322
msgid ""
"This one first takes the percentage in two decimal behind the comma for both "
"layers. It then adds the two values. Divides 2 by the sum."
msgstr ""
"Detta tar först procentvärdet med två decimaler efter kommatecknet för båda "
"lagren, och adderar därefter de två värdena. Dividerar summan med 2."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:329
msgid ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Parallel_Sample_image_with_dots.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: images/blending_modes/mix/"
"Blending_modes_Parallel_Sample_image_with_dots.png"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:329
msgid "Left: **Normal**. Right: **Parallel**."
msgstr "Vänster: **Normal**. Höger: **Parallel**."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:331
#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:335
msgid "Penumbra A"
msgstr "Halvskugga A"

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:339
msgid "This blending mode is called \"Penumbra A\" in English."
msgstr "Blandningsläget kallas \"Penumbra A\" på engelska."

#: ../../reference_manual/blending_modes/mix.rst:341
msgid ""
"Creates a linear penumbra falloff. This means most tones will be in the "
"midtone ranges."
msgstr ""
"Skapar en linjär avtagande halvskugga. Det betyder att de flesta toner är i "
"medelintervallet."

